# This file exists only to keep the empty ``static/`` directory tracked by
# Git.  Git does not track empty directories; an empty placeholder file is
# the standard idiom for preserving the directory structure in a repository.
#
# Role
# ====
#
# This directory is a **candidate** for the ``frontend.static_dir``
# setting in :class:`nexusdl.core.config.Settings`. When that setting
# points here (rare — most deployments serve the frontend from Next.js,
# nginx, Caddy or another CDN), FastAPI mounts it at ``/`` with
# ``html=True`` via
# :func:`nexusdl.interfaces.web.backend.main._mount_static`. In the
# default configuration the setting is unset, so this directory is
# **never** mounted — it exists purely to give deployments a place to
# drop a pre-built static frontend without inventing their own path.
#
# The default static frontend shipped with NexusDL is the Next.js
# application under ``src/nexusdl/interfaces/web/frontend/``. Its
# exported assets (``.next``, ``out/``, or wherever the deployment
# points ``frontend.static_dir``) are what ``_mount_static`` serves when
# the operator opts into backend-hosted static serving. Nothing in this
# directory is bundled with the Python package by default.
#
# It is intentionally empty in the source tree: any real assets are
# added by the deployment, not committed here. This keeps the wheel /
# sdist small and lets the deployment choose between Next.js dev server,
# a pre-built SPA, or a CDN — without changing the source tree.
#
# Do not delete this file unless the directory is populated with a
# tracked asset. Do not add content here: this placeholder must remain
# harmless if accidentally served by the static file handler (it
# contains only comments — no executable content, no secrets, no data).
#
# If you are looking for the assets served by the *default* deployment,
# see ``src/nexusdl/interfaces/web/frontend/public/`` (favicons, logos,
# screenshots, manifest, og-image, etc.).
